@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Variant - the same system modeled with SysML blocks (value/part/flow properties, ports) vs UML classes (attributes/operations).
'   usecase:      Note the SysML-specific features absent from a plain UML class diagram.
'   complexity:   medium
'   domain:       Diagram-family comparison
' ============================================================================
title Example SysML Block BDD (Variant) - Block vs Class

' SysML BLOCKS: value properties (typed w/ units), part properties (composition),
'   flow/proxy/full ports, flow properties with direction, requirement links.
' UML CLASSES: attributes + operations + associations; no ports/flow/units natively.

block "PumpBlock" {
  value flowRate : Real [L/min]
  port out "pumpOut" : ICoolantFlow
  flow in  supply : Coolant
  flow out return : Coolant
}

class "PumpClass" {
  -flowRate : double
  +start() : void
  +stop() : void
}

note
  SysML block adds: typed value properties with units, ports (flow/proxy/full),
  and flow properties with direction. The UML class has attributes and operations
  but no native notion of ports, flows, or physical units.
end note

@enduml
